  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 117 PM CDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nMoisture from Tropical Storm Vance will continue advecting into the \nregion promoting isolated to scattered showers across the Brush \nCountry. Some showers could be heavy at times which could leading to \nponding of water or flash flooding. WPC currently has La Salle and \nWebb counties under a Marginal Risk of excessive rainfall. We'll dry \nout this weekend for a warm and humid Halloween before our next cool \ndown early next week. Models continue to trend the frontal passage \naround Tuesday. There is currently a low to medium chance for \nshowers and thunderstorms across the Coastal Bend and Victoria \nCrossroads with the best chances across the latter. \n\nCoastal flooding is expected to continue tonight into early tomorrow \nmorning with an elevated risk of rip currents. Water levels are \nexpected to remain below coastal flooding thresholds tomorrow, but \nwe will further evaluate it later tonight and tomorrow morning.",
